<p class="mb-4"><strong>Why pick Luna:</strong> it's the only GPT-5.6 tier under $1/M input. Use it for autocomplete, docstring generation, test scaffolding, and the high-volume low-stakes tasks where you'd otherwise burn GPT-5.6 Sol credits.</p>

<p class="mb-4"><strong>Why avoid Luna:</strong> it's the weakest GPT-5.6 variant — the input/cached ratio (10x cache discount) suggests aggressive quantization or distillation. For refactors, multi-file edits, and architectural reasoning, step up to Sol or Terra.</p>

<p class="mb-4"><strong>Setup cost:</strong> two minutes. Create an OpenAI platform account, add a payment method, generate a key at <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded text-sm">platform.openai.com/api-keys</code>, paste it into Cursor's settings → Models → OpenAI API Key. Works from Nov 13 onward without changes.</p>

<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Route 2: Switch to Anthropic Claude Opus 5 / Sonnet 5 (Cursor native)</h3>

<p class="mb-4">Cursor already supports Anthropic Claude natively — and Anthropic explicitly signaled continuity. Tom Brown (Anthropic co-founder and Chief Compute Officer) on X, Friday night Aug 28/29: <em>"Cursor has been a trusted partner of Anthropic since Sonnet 3.5. We'll continue to increase compute to support Claude models in Cursor and are excited for what comes next with them at SpaceX."</em> Both CNBC and the-decoder.com reproduce the quote.</p>

