<p class="mb-4"><strong>Why pick Opus 5:</strong> it's the strongest coding model Cursor currently supports natively, with 1M context window. Best for cross-file refactors, architectural decisions, and code review of complex PRs.</p>

<p class="mb-4"><strong>Why pick Sonnet 5:</strong> 60% cheaper than Opus on input, ~50% the cost on output. Sonnet has been Cursor's workhorse for two years; on coding benchmarks it sits within 8-15% of Opus while costing roughly half.</p>

<p class="mb-4"><strong>Setup cost:</strong> one minute. Add Anthropic as a provider in Cursor's settings, paste your Anthropic API key from <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded text-sm">console.anthropic.com</code>. Cursor already routes Sonnet 4.5 today; Opus 5 / Sonnet 5 should appear in the model picker once Anthropic rolls out the model IDs.</p>

