<p class="mb-4"><strong>Why pick Workers AI:</strong> edge caching makes Tab autocomplete feel instant, 10K Neurons/day free for low-volume users, and the open-weights lineup (GLM-5.3, Kimi K2.7-Code, Llama 3.3 70B, GPT-OSS 120B) is competitive with closed-source peers at half the cost. Cursor already supports custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints, so pointing at <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded text-sm">https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/&lt;id&gt;/ai/v1</code> works.</p>

<p class="mb-4"><strong>Watch out:</strong> frontier models on Workers AI (GLM-5.3, GLM-5.2, Kimi K2.7-Code) require Workers Paid ($5/month) or prepaid AI Gateway credits — no free tier for these. Also, the rate-limit table for frontier models is still settling as of 2026-09-01.</p>

<h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Route 5: Google Gemini Flash (the sub-$1 frontier option)</h3>

<p class="mb-4">If you want frontier-tier quality without frontier-tier pricing, Google's Gemini Flash family is the standout. All three tiers ship on OpenRouter and direct via Google AI Studio, all with 1M context, all under $1/M input:</p>

